evel I.S.P. is printed. || COMBAT: two attacks per melee round plus those of the hand to hand training, stored as bonuses.combat.attacks 2. Most males are 3rd to 9th level (2D4+1) describes NPCs and is not stored. || SKILLS COMMON TO BOTH (parent list): Running, Climbing (40, no bonus), W.P. Knife, and the six player character skills as one choice of six from the printed list with no bonus: Pilot Motorcycle is Motorcycles & Snowmobiles, Pilot Automobile is Automobile, Pilot Hover Craft is Hover Craft (ground), pilot sail or motor boat is Boat: Sail Type and Boat: Motor, Race & Hydrofoil, Monster Lore is Lore: Demons & Monsters, Faerie Lore is Lore: Faeries & Creatures of Magic, any languages is the catalog''s Rifts tongues plus Language: Other. || MALES: All wilderness skills (+20%) stored as the nine Wilderness skills of the Rifts main rule book list (judgement; Wilderness rows added by later books - Dowsing, Fasting, Spelunking and the sea skills - are left out): Boat Building 25+20, Carpentry 25+20, Hunting, Identify Plants & Fruit 25+20, Land Navigation 36+20, Preserve Food 25+20, Skin & Prepare Animal Hides 30+20, Track & Trap Animals 20+20, and Wilderness Survival at its own printed +30 (30+30 = 60). Track (humanoids; +20%) is Tracking (people) 25+20. Horsemanship (and monstermanship; +20%) stored as Horsemanship: General 40+20 and Horsemanship: Exotic Animals 30+20 (judgement: monstermanship is riding monsters, which the catalog files as exotic animals). Dance 30 and Sing 35, no bonus. Hand to Hand: Assassin, Body Building, General Athletics (catalog Athletics (general)), three other Physical skills except Boxing and Acrobatics. W.P. Archery and Targeting is the catalog''s two rows W.P. Archery and W.P. Targeting; W.P. Energy Rifle; three W.P.s of choice. || FEMALES: All domestic (+30%) stored as the six Domestic skills of the Rifts main rule book list (judgement, as above): Cook 35+30, Dance 30+30, Fishing 40+30, Sewing 40+30, Sing 35+30, Play Musical Instrument 35+30. Wilderness skills (+10%) the same nine at +10, Wilderness Survival at its printed +15 (45). Horsemanship with no bonus: General 40, Exotic Animals 30. Holistic Medicine 20+20. Hand to Hand: Basic, two other Physical skills (no exclusion printed for females), W.P. Blunt, two other W.P.s. || NOT PRINTED: no related or secondary skills, no hand to hand upgrade price, no language line (a language is one of the six optional picks), no money line, no cybernetics line, no saving throw bonuses; nothing stored for any of them. || EQUIPMENT: Knife (knife); two energy weapons with no model named, stored as two choices from catalog energy pistols and rifles (judgement); light mega-damage body armor (light-mdc-body-armor), backpack, a couple of sacks (sack x2), utility/ammo-belt (utility-ammo-belt), gun holster, binoculars, air filter or gas mask as a choice. Perhaps bow and arrows, the favorite weapons (vibro-blades, mega-damage arrows, magic hand-held weapons) and personal items are prose in GM Notes. The riding animal (a horse or an Ostrosaurus) is a natural ability line, not gear. || XP: the ladder headed Monkey Boy Tech, Simvan Monster Rider on the unnumbered Experience Tables page after printed 174 (cache p176). || TAGS: combat, hunter and wilderness for the males the book describes as warriors, trackers and hunters; healer for the females, who are the tribe''s psychic healers. Not evil: the alignment line is aberrant evil, or any."
